  "novel_mechanics_found": "Confirmed the load-bearing paint-then-route mechanic for level 8. A 22x4 outline must be shifted left to x=3..24 before descending from its color swatch; at x=6..27, collision adjacency reaches the neighboring swatch and silently repaints it. Applying that safety shift independently to the color-11 and color-6 rectangles, then using the y=15..18 corridor, compressing to 4x22 at the upper fixture, crossing the x=44..49 opening, and restoring at the lower fixture placed both target geometries simultaneously and advanced to level 8.",
  "narrative": "Resolved the 519-action level-7 prefix through resolve_replay_plan, replayed it from a fresh env.reset(), and directly confirmed frame_level(frame)==7. I then executed a corrected 170-action level-8 tail: paint and safely route the color-11 rectangle to x=9..15,y=39..57, select the second rectangle, paint it color 6 with the same one-step safety margin, route it through the corridor/opening, and restore it to 16x10. The second rectangle triggered the live 7->8 transition at full-sequence action 689. One already-queued post-win diagnostic action was also sent (session call 690) and encountered the empty terminal frame; the periodic checkpoint had already preserved the exact 689-action winning line. Only 10 calls remained, far fewer than the 689 needed for a fresh-reset reproduction gate, so reproduction_verified is honestly false.",
  "gotchas": [
    "The first 519 actions exactly match results/outer_loop_fable5_re86_probe.json and were freshly replayed to frame_level 7 in this session.",
    "For both wide 22x4 rectangles, paint at the intended swatch and shift to x=3..24 before moving vertically into or out of the paint row. The tempting x=6..27 position is adjacency-unsafe and caused the round-6 null.",
    "The safe transit lattice is x=36..57,y=15..18 before upper-fixture compression; the actual palette-wall opening is x=44..49.",
    "The color-11 target is a 7x19 outline at x=9..15,y=39..57. The color-6 target is a 16x10 outline at x=6..21,y=45..54.",
    "The win occurred on action 689, during the eighth final ACTION3 after four restoration ACTION2 moves for the color-6 rectangle. Two further ACTION3 moves from the queued batch are not part of the checkpointed candidate.",
    "A post-win frame may be an empty grid; compact numpy diff code must shape-check before comparing it with the preceding 64x64 frame.",
    "The session used 690 env.step calls total: 519 prefix, 170 actions through the live win, and one already-queued post-win diagnostic call."
